35,2,1,talk,Asuka,,"The morning rush is more chaotic than it seems; people are already shifting other bikes to get out. Also, the rain exposure is uneven, with some spots staying wet overnight.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,"The building account is quite bare, covering only basics. Any new infrastructure would require a levy, and the current cash collection process is already a time-consuming burden for the treasurer.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,George,,"It seems the covered spots have been held by the same flats for years without any formal review. Also, some daily riders are actually willing to pay a fee rather than just having an equal claim.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,"It's fascinating how we ignore the small things until they pile up. Our own logs are full of vague complaints about leaning bikes, and the neighbors learned the hard way that fees can turn neighbors into strangers.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Mio,,"It's a lot more work than I thought! The treasurer is already spending hours on cash, and the sticker register shows some people have way more bikes than others. We have to be careful not to make the job impossible!","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"@George, if some people have held the best spots for years, that explains why the rain exposure is such an issue for others. It's not just about space, but the quality of the space.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Mio, I agree. If the treasurer is already spending three hours a month on basic collections, adding a complex per-place billing system would be an unreasonable administrative burden.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,George,,It is concerning that the arrangement hasn't been reviewed in five years. It suggests a lack of transparency that likely fuels the resentment some residents are feeling about who gets the best spots.,"{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Ryuji, you're right about the burden, but let's not forget the social cost. If we introduce fees to solve the shortage, we might just end up with people avoiding each other in the lobby.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Mio,,"@Shunichi, I get that, but if we don't fix it, people will just keep complaining! Maybe there's a way to keep it simple so it doesn't feel like a business transaction?","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Asuka,,"If we want to avoid social friction, we must address the physical chaos. Shifting other people's bikes in the morning is a recipe for conflict, regardless of whether we charge a fee or not.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,"We should avoid any solution that requires a new levy or complex billing. The ledger shows we have no surplus, and the treasurer is already stretched thin. Simplicity is the only way to ensure sustainability.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,George,,"I agree that simplicity is key, but we cannot ignore the fact that the current system is stagnant. If we don't address the long-term occupancy of the best spots, the friction will only grow.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,"@George, transparency is a fine goal, but let's not mistake a ""formal review"" for a solution. If we start auditing every spot, we're just inviting people to fight over a few inches of dry pavement.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Mio,,"@Asuka, you're right about the chaos! If we make the rules too complicated, we'll just be adding more paperwork to the treasurer's plate and more fighting in the parking lot. Let's find something easy to manage!","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Asuka,,"We need a system that prioritizes physical order over administrative complexity. If we can organize the layout to stop the shoving matches and rain issues, we solve the root cause of the friction.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Ryuji,,"I agree with Asuka. If we focus on the physical organization and avoid introducing new fees or levies, we protect both the building's finances and the treasurer's time. A low-maintenance system is the most rational choice.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,George,,"While I agree with the need for low maintenance, we must ensure the new system is fair. If we simply reorganize the layout without addressing the long-term occupancy, we are just rearranging the same grievances.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Shunichi,,"Fairness is a slippery slope, George. If we try to engineer a ""perfectly fair"" system, we'll likely just create a new set of grievances. I'd rather have a bit of stagnation than a building full of people who stop speaking.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Mio,,I think we're all agreeing that we can't make this a second full-time job for whoever is in charge! Let's keep it light and simple so it actually lasts this time.,"{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":true,""norm"":[{""code"":""trailing_over"",""token"":""Over"",""tail"":""Over""}]}"
55,2,4,pass,Mio,,Over,"{""forced"":false,""empty"":false,""trailing"":true}"
